αλός ἐστι"],["we are friends","philoi esmen","PHEE-loy ES-men","φίλοι ἐσμέν"],["they are men","andres eisi","AN-dres eh-SEE","ἄνδρες εἰσί"]]},{"id":"to-be-eimi","title":"To be: eimi","text":["The verb \"to be\" is irregular: eimi, ei, esti, esmen, este, eisi. The verb often comes after the noun, as in \"mathetes eimi\"."],"rows":[["I am","eimi","εἰμί"],["you are","ei","εἶ"],["he / she is","esti","ἐστί"],["we are","esmen","ἐσμέν"],["you are (plural)","este","ἐστέ"],["they are","eisi","εἰσί"]],"ex":[["I am a man","aner eimi","ah-NAIR eh-MEE","ἀνήρ εἰμι"],["you are good","agathos ei","ah-gah-THOS AY","ἀγαθὸς εἶ"],["he is in the house","en to oiko esti","en toh OY-koh ES-tee","ἐν τῷ οἴκῳ ἐστί"],["we are in the city","en te polei esmen","en tay POH-lay ES-men","ἐν τῇ πόλει ἐσμέν"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"ou\" before the verb to deny a fact. \"Ouk\" is used before a vowel. \"Me\" is used for commands, wishes and conditions."],"rows":[["not (fact)","ou / ouk","οὐ / οὐκ"],["not (command or wish)","me","μή"]],"ex":[["I know","oida","OY-dah","οἶδα"],["I do not know","ouk oida","OOK OY-dah","οὐκ οἶδα"],["he is good","agathos esti","ah-gah-THOS ES-tee","ἀγαθός ἐστι"],["he is not good","ouk agathos esti","OOK ah-gah-THOS ES-tee","οὐκ ἀγαθός ἐστι"],["do not say","me lege","MAY LEH-geh","μὴ λέγε"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["The second-person singular command is usually the bare stem: lege (say!), grapse (write!). Plural adds -ete: legete."],"rows":[["say!","lege","λέγε"],["write!","grapse","γράψον"],["come!","deuro","δεῦρο"]],"ex":[["come here","deuro","DEH-oo-ro","δεῦρο"],["say","lege","LEH-geh","λέγε"],["listen","akoue","ah-KOO-eh","ἄκουε"],["wait","mene","MEH-neh","μένε"]]},{"id":"questions","title":"Questions","text":["Add \"ara\" at the start for a yes or no question, or use a question word."],"rows":[["Is it...?","ara","ἆρα"]],"ex":[["is he a teacher?","ara didaskalos esti","AH-rah dee-DAS-kah-los ES-tee","ἆρα διδάσκαλός ἐστι;"],["what is this?","ti esti touto","tee ES-tee TOO-toh","τί ἐστι τοῦτο;"],["who are you?","tis ei","TIS AY","τίς εἶ;"]]}],"name":"Ancient Greek","id":"grc","flag":"gr","script":"Greek","note":""}